WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.146 --> 00:00:00.979
(people cheering)

00:00:00.979 --> 00:00:03.450
- [Narrator] The defending
champion US Women's Soccer team

00:00:03.450 --> 00:00:05.370
is going into their first World Cup

00:00:05.370 --> 00:00:07.290
since agreeing to share their prize money

00:00:07.290 --> 00:00:09.330
with the US Men's team.

00:00:09.330 --> 00:00:10.680
- It's just gonna be very competitive.

00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:13.890
It's gonna be the most watched World Cup.

00:00:13.890 --> 00:00:15.540
It's gonna be the best one yet.

00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:16.500
- [Narrator] The Americans are going

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:17.970
after an unprecedented

00:00:17.970 --> 00:00:20.550
third consecutive World Cup championship.

00:00:20.550 --> 00:00:23.880
But that's not the only
goal on players' minds.

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:25.800
- There's still a big discrepancy

00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:27.420
between the men's prize money

00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:30.210
from FIFA and the women's, and
to me, that's unacceptable.

00:00:30.210 --> 00:00:32.850
- [Narrator] FIFA is a
nonprofit organization.

00:00:32.850 --> 00:00:35.820
This year, they've more than
tripled the total prize money

00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:38.610
for the Women's World
Cup compared to 2019.

00:00:38.610 --> 00:00:42.120
But the $110 million
announced by FIFA in March

00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:45.540
is a fraction of what the
men received just last year.

00:00:45.540 --> 00:00:47.400
- We still have a lot of fight left

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:49.500
and there's a lot of room for improvement.

00:00:51.319 --> 00:00:55.020
(team chanting indistinctly)

00:00:55.020 --> 00:00:56.820
- The US is the most successful team

00:00:56.820 --> 00:00:58.890
in FIFA Women's World Cup history,

00:00:58.890 --> 00:01:00.900
winning the tournament four times.

00:01:00.900 --> 00:01:03.120
The only team with more World Cup Gold

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:06.570
is Brazil's men's team with five titles.

00:01:06.570 --> 00:01:09.510
US Forward Christen Press
won back-to-back titles

00:01:09.510 --> 00:01:11.640
in 2015 and 2019

00:01:11.640 --> 00:01:14.040
but has been sidelined
for a year with an injury.

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:15.990
- When we won the World Cup in 2015,

00:01:15.990 --> 00:01:17.310
it became abundantly clear

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:19.020
that the way that we were being valued

00:01:19.020 --> 00:01:22.020
by our employer did not match
the way that we were valued

00:01:22.020 --> 00:01:23.190
by the world.

00:01:23.190 --> 00:01:25.530
- [Narrator] Press is one of
the players who filed a lawsuit

00:01:25.530 --> 00:01:27.240
against the US Soccer Federation

00:01:27.240 --> 00:01:29.400
for gender discrimination just ahead

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:32.220
of the 2019 tournament in France.

00:01:32.220 --> 00:01:33.330
- When you play in a World Cup,

00:01:33.330 --> 00:01:35.640
you really shut out the world.

00:01:35.640 --> 00:01:39.690
You have to be dedicated and
focused entirely on your craft

00:01:39.690 --> 00:01:41.280
on what happens between the lines.

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:42.810
But yet we had that drum beat

00:01:42.810 --> 00:01:46.500
in the back of our minds that
this was for something bigger.

00:01:46.500 --> 00:01:47.940
- [Narrator] The lawsuit alleges a number

00:01:47.940 --> 00:01:49.170
of inequalities compared

00:01:49.170 --> 00:01:51.750
to the men's team,
including pay disparities,

00:01:51.750 --> 00:01:54.093
training conditions, and game promotion.

00:01:54.930 --> 00:01:57.630
In its response, the US
Soccer Federation argued

00:01:57.630 --> 00:02:00.030
that the men's and women's
team were not comparable

00:02:00.030 --> 00:02:01.590
because of their different schedules,

00:02:01.590 --> 00:02:03.870
obligations, and compensation

00:02:03.870 --> 00:02:06.150
and that the women's
team had no counterparts

00:02:06.150 --> 00:02:07.620
on the men's team.

00:02:07.620 --> 00:02:09.570
The US Soccer Federation did not reply

00:02:09.570 --> 00:02:11.565
to a request for comment.

00:02:11.565 --> 00:02:13.920
- [Crowd] Equal pay, equal pay, equal pay.

00:02:13.920 --> 00:02:15.660
- [Narrator] After a
three-year legal battle,

00:02:15.660 --> 00:02:19.860
the players and US Soccer
reached a $24 million settlement.

00:02:19.860 --> 00:02:22.860
Both the men's and the women's
team reached new labor deals

00:02:22.860 --> 00:02:25.830
with US Soccer that
aligned the team's pay.

00:02:25.830 --> 00:02:27.960
The two teams also agreed to pool

00:02:27.960 --> 00:02:29.370
and share their prize money

00:02:29.370 --> 00:02:31.113
from their respective World Cups.

00:02:34.017 --> 00:02:35.070
(lively music)

00:02:35.070 --> 00:02:37.410
This year's tournament
will include more teams,

00:02:37.410 --> 00:02:40.743
more prize money, and more
fanfare than ever before.

00:02:41.580 --> 00:02:44.208
The Women's World Cup debuted in 1991,

00:02:44.208 --> 00:02:47.070
61 years after the first men's tournament.

00:02:47.070 --> 00:02:48.000
In recent years,

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:50.760
the women's event has made
large gains in viewers

00:02:50.760 --> 00:02:54.660
but its prize money remains far
behind the men's tournament.

00:02:54.660 --> 00:02:57.270
FIFA says the 2019 Women's World Cup

00:02:57.270 --> 00:03:00.900
in France drew 1.1
billion viewers worldwide,

00:03:00.900 --> 00:03:04.410
31% of the almost 3.6 billion people

00:03:04.410 --> 00:03:07.830
who watched the 2018
Men's World Cup in Russia

00:03:07.830 --> 00:03:10.938
but it awarded the women just 7.5%

00:03:10.938 --> 00:03:15.330
of the $400 million prize
money that it awarded the men.

00:03:15.330 --> 00:03:16.710
In June, FIFA announced

00:03:16.710 --> 00:03:19.170
that for the first time
in a Women's World Cup,

00:03:19.170 --> 00:03:22.440
a portion of the prize money
would be earmarked specifically

00:03:22.440 --> 00:03:23.370
for the players.

00:03:23.370 --> 00:03:26.340
In the past, federations
generally decided how much

00:03:26.340 --> 00:03:28.650
of the prize money to give players.

00:03:28.650 --> 00:03:31.380
In a statement, FIFA
president Gianni Infantino

00:03:31.380 --> 00:03:34.410
called the distribution
model unprecedented.

00:03:34.410 --> 00:03:37.530
Each player will earn a minimum of $30,000

00:03:37.530 --> 00:03:41.910
with the women on the winning
team getting $270,000.

00:03:41.910 --> 00:03:46.740
- Having them direct payments
to the players is huge.

00:03:46.740 --> 00:03:48.000
I mean, it's a life-changing thing

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:49.620
for some of these players.

00:03:49.620 --> 00:03:52.080
- [Narrator] The payment
model for 2023 was welcomed

00:03:52.080 --> 00:03:54.450
by FIFPRO, an umbrella organization

00:03:54.450 --> 00:03:56.820
that represents 65,000 men's

00:03:56.820 --> 00:04:00.180
and women's soccer players
and their unions worldwide.

00:04:00.180 --> 00:04:02.190
- The biggest thing probably
at the minute is making sure

00:04:02.190 --> 00:04:05.640
that the agreement, the
conditions, the compensation system

00:04:05.640 --> 00:04:07.620
that we were able to put in place together

00:04:07.620 --> 00:04:10.034
with FIFA are actually being implemented.

00:04:10.034 --> 00:04:12.480
(pensive music)

00:04:12.480 --> 00:04:14.130
- [Narrator] Because of a unique mechanism

00:04:14.130 --> 00:04:16.290
in their collective bargaining agreements,

00:04:16.290 --> 00:04:18.720
whatever the American women win this year,

00:04:18.720 --> 00:04:21.180
they'll share with the US men's team.

00:04:21.180 --> 00:04:22.620
It works like this.

00:04:22.620 --> 00:04:25.230
Let's say the US women take first place.

00:04:25.230 --> 00:04:28.410
FIFA has allotted $4.29 million

00:04:28.410 --> 00:04:32.250
in prize money for the 2023
winning member association.

00:04:32.250 --> 00:04:34.890
In this example, that's US Soccer.

00:04:34.890 --> 00:04:39.150
Each of the 23 players on
the roster gets $270,000.

00:04:39.150 --> 00:04:42.330
That's another $6.21 million.

00:04:42.330 --> 00:04:45.570
Combined, that's $10.5 million from FIFA

00:04:45.570 --> 00:04:47.610
for winning the Women's World Cup.

00:04:47.610 --> 00:04:48.840
For the Americans,

00:04:48.840 --> 00:04:51.990
that money would get pooled
with what the US Men's team won

00:04:51.990 --> 00:04:55.080
for reaching the knockout stage
in their World Cup last year

00:04:55.080 --> 00:04:58.500
for a total of $23.5 million.

00:04:58.500 --> 00:05:01.650
A portion of that goes to
the US Soccer Federation

00:05:01.650 --> 00:05:04.413
and the men's and women's
teams split the rest.

00:05:05.807 --> 00:05:07.290
(lively music)

00:05:07.290 --> 00:05:10.260
FIFA says it's modernizing
football to be global,

00:05:10.260 --> 00:05:13.620
accessible and inclusive in all aspects.

00:05:13.620 --> 00:05:16.080
In a video posted on
social media just days

00:05:16.080 --> 00:05:18.360
before the 2023 World Cup kickoff,

00:05:18.360 --> 00:05:21.240
players from co-host country
Australia highlighted the gap

00:05:21.240 --> 00:05:22.380
in FIFA prize money

00:05:22.380 --> 00:05:25.140
between the men's and
women's competitions.

00:05:25.140 --> 00:05:26.820
- Collective bargaining has allowed us

00:05:26.820 --> 00:05:30.180
to ensure we now get the same
conditions as the Socceroos

00:05:30.180 --> 00:05:31.530
with one exception.

00:05:31.530 --> 00:05:34.140
FIFA will still only offer women 1/4

00:05:34.140 --> 00:05:36.990
as much prize money as men
for the same achievement.

00:05:36.990 --> 00:05:38.880
- [Narrator] FIFA says
it's aiming for equality

00:05:38.880 --> 00:05:43.050
in the prize money for the
2026/2027 World Cup cycle.

00:05:43.050 --> 00:05:46.230
That would be a 300%
increase for the women

00:05:46.230 --> 00:05:49.860
if the men's prize money
remains at 440 million.

00:05:49.860 --> 00:05:53.430
- We're seeing growth across
the globe in the women's game

00:05:53.430 --> 00:05:55.440
at a league level, at
an international level.

00:05:55.440 --> 00:05:58.020
The support's there, and
I think that is going

00:05:58.020 --> 00:06:00.378
to make it the the best World Cup ever.

00:06:00.378 --> 00:06:03.045
(pensive music)

